        "problem": "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{3}$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Q\\cdot {I}_{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |  |",
